Out of curiosity, how do you think it's mis-named?

All of those trophies except the Full Monty were named for a sports term
referring to a number.  In the case of "hat trick", it refers to a bowler in
cricket who takes "three 
wickets with three successive balls" (see
<http://www.worldwidewords.org/qa/qa-hat1.htm>, not that I know exactly what
that means.  ;-)

The trophy has 3 requirements, hence "hat trick".  We weren't really strick
about the naming, but we did make sure each one did actually have a clear
numerical connection to its name.

In that vein a "birdie" is a golf term for shooting a hole 1 under par; a
"double top" is a darts term for the double-20 space; a "grand slam" is a
baseball term for a batter hitting a home run with the bases loaded and thus
scoring four points.

In case anyone was curious where those names came from ... ;-)

